# The expression x*x*x + 2*x is represented as a tree of sum, product and leaf terms.
# Derives its symbolic derivative by the sum and product rules, then evaluates it at x = 0 and 3.
# Concludes slopes of 2 and 29. Shows structural recursion, repeated-variable matching,
# constructed terms and exact evaluation, without parsing arbitrary algebraic prose.

sum(product(variable(x), product(variable(x), variable(x))), product(constant(2), variable(x))) is a formula.
x is a differentiationVariable.
point(x, 0) and point(x, 3).

# Visit only subexpressions of the supplied formula, keeping symbolic construction finite.
For every E, if E is a formula then E is an expression.
For every A and B, if sum(A, B) is an expression then A is an expression and B is an expression.
For every A and B, if product(A, B) is an expression then A is an expression and B is an expression.

# A variable's derivative is one; constants contribute zero.
For every X,
if variable(X) is an expression and X is a differentiationVariable
then derivative(variable(X), X, constant(1)).
For every N and X,
if constant(N) is an expression and X is a differentiationVariable
then derivative(constant(N), X, constant(0)).

# Construct derivative trees without feeding those new trees back into differentiation.
For every A and B and X and U and V,
if sum(A, B) is an expression and derivative(A, X, U) and derivative(B, X, V)
then derivative(sum(A, B), X, sum(U, V)).
For every A and B and X and U and V,
if product(A, B) is an expression and derivative(A, X, U) and derivative(B, X, V)
then derivative(product(A, B), X, sum(product(U, B), product(A, V))).

# Evaluation has its own finite tree domain: the final derivative and its subterms.
For every E and X and D,
if E is a formula and derivative(E, X, D) then D is evaluable.
For every A and B, if sum(A, B) is evaluable then A is evaluable and B is evaluable.
For every A and B, if product(A, B) is evaluable then A is evaluable and B is evaluable.
For every N and X and P,
if constant(N) is evaluable and point(X, P) then evaluated(constant(N), X, P, N).
For every X and P,
if variable(X) is evaluable and point(X, P) then evaluated(variable(X), X, P, P).
For every A and B and X and P and U and V and N,
if sum(A, B) is evaluable and evaluated(A, X, P, U) and evaluated(B, X, P, V)
and N is the value of U + V then evaluated(sum(A, B), X, P, N).
For every A and B and X and P and U and V and N,
if product(A, B) is evaluable and evaluated(A, X, P, U) and evaluated(B, X, P, V)
and N is the value of U * V then evaluated(product(A, B), X, P, N).

# Include the symbolic tree as evidence as well as its numeric slope.
For every E and X and D and P and N,
if E is a formula and derivative(E, X, D) and evaluated(D, X, P, N)
then analysis(E, D, P, N).
Find every E and D and P and N such that analysis(E, D, P, N).
